direction: down

vars: {
  d2-config: {
    theme-id: 0
    layout-engine: dagre
    pad: 40
  }
}

classes: {
  ext: {
    style.fill: "#eceff1"
    style.stroke: "#90a4ae"
  }
  go: {
    style.fill: "#e3f2fd"
    style.stroke: "#1976d2"
  }
  lib: {
    style.fill: "#e0f2f1"
    style.stroke: "#00897b"
  }
  ctl: {
    style.fill: "#e5e7eb"
    style.stroke: "#37474f"
  }
  bad: {
    style.fill: "#ffebee"
    style.stroke: "#c62828"
  }
}

guard: "core/metrics/naming.go\nthe mft_ rule, enforced where a\nmetric is created\nEight constructors, one rule: Counter ·\nCounterVec · Gauge · GaugeVec · Histogram ·\nHistogramVec · DurationHistogram ·\nDurationHistogramVec.\nThe helpers are opt-in — a component on\npromauto.With(reg) keeps working, and the\nonly thing still reviewed is the name it\nregisters." {
  class: lib

  validate: "ValidateName, then newSpec, before any\nregistry is touched\n1. Prefix mft_ — or ErrMissingPrefix,\n   whose message names what it expected:\n   mft_ + the name you passed\n2. the Prometheus name grammar: a letter,\n   underscore or colon first, then\n   letters, digits, underscores, colons\n3. a non-empty Help, the only\n   documentation the metric will ever have\nMustRegister adds the third programmer\nerror: a duplicate already on the registry,\nfrom reg.Register returning\nAlreadyRegisteredError." {
    class: go
  }

  panic: "must(err) -> panic(err) — naming.go:91\nThe deliberate choice, and the one rule\nthat makes the rest mean something. A\nmetric that scrapes under a foreign name\nis a series nobody watches and nobody is\npaged for, and it stays that way until\nsomebody notices a panel that stopped\nmoving. A service that refuses to start is\na five-minute fix at 09:00. The panic is\nat REGISTRATION, not at first use, so\nnothing trades a minute against it." {
    class: bad
  }

  unit: "DurationHistogram and\nDurationHistogramVec take\nnewDurationSpec, which adds\nValidateDurationName: a latency name\nmust end in _seconds, or the error\nsays the unit is ambiguous.\nThe unit belongs in the name, not in a\ncomment." {
    class: go
  }

  validate -> panic: "a violation stops the process\ninstead of shipping a series\nnobody is watching"
  validate -> unit: "plus the suffix, for latency\nnames only"
}

latency: "core/metrics/latency.go\nseconds, and the join from a metric\nto a log line" {
  class: lib

  observe: "ObserveDuration(h, start, id) -> time.Duration\nd.Seconds() is what lands in the bucket\n— seconds, matching the name — and the\nduration is returned so the call fits a\ndefer. When id is non-empty and h is a\nprometheus.ExemplarObserver the value is\nrecorded with ObserveWithExemplar,\nlabels trace_id = id; otherwise it falls\nback to a plain Observe.\nDefaultBuckets: 0.5ms, 1ms, 2.5ms, 5ms,\n10ms, 25ms, 50ms, 100ms, 250ms, 500ms,\n1s, 2.5s, 5s, 10s, 30s — cache reads\nthrough backfill runs.\nAn exemplar, never a label: a correlation\nid as a label is unbounded cardinality,\nand METRICS.md rule 6 forbids it by name." {
    class: go
  }

  om: "Handler(reg) sets\nEnableOpenMetrics: true\nWithout it the exemplar stops at the\nprocess boundary and the id is lost.\nPrometheus v3 negotiates OpenMetrics\nby default, the other half of why the\ncompose file pins v3.0.1." {
    class: ctl
  }

  observe -> om: "only survives the scrape if the\nexposition is OpenMetrics"
}

build: "core/metrics/buildinfo.go\nwhich commit was running when\nthis alert fired" {
  class: lib

  buildinfo: "RegisterBuildInfo(reg, BuildInfo)\nbuildinfo.go:41\nmft_build_info, a gauge held at 1, with\nthe metadata as const labels:\nservice · version · commit · branch ·\ngoversion · env\nmft_uptime_seconds, a GaugeFunc over\ntime.Since(processStart)\nEmpty version, commit and branch are\nfilled from debug.ReadBuildInfo —\nvcs.revision, vcs.modified appends\n-dirty, vcs.ref loses refs/heads/ — and\nthen default to 'unknown', so even a\nplain go run produces a complete, honest\nseries. goversion defaults to\nruntime.Version(). It returns its error\ninstead of panicking: a second call in\none process is a wiring mistake, not a\ntypo." {
    class: go
  }

  nocall: "GAP — no service calls\nRegisterBuildInfo\nEvery cmd/server is core.Module plus\nthe service's own module, and neither\nregisters build info. The Grafana\nPlatform row queries mft_build_info and\nmft_uptime_seconds, so both panels are\nempty and the first question the\nobservability README tells you to ask —\nwhich commit produced this? — has no\nseries to answer it. One fx.Invoke in the\nshared core module would close it." {
    class: bad
  }
}

health: "core/metrics/health.go\nliveness that cannot fail,\nreadiness that can" {
  class: lib

  mux: "Mux(cfg, scrape) — metrics.go:58\ncfg.Metrics.Path (default /metrics) gets\nthe scrape handler, and unless that\npath is / the same mux also gets\nNewHealth(cfg.App.Name, DefaultChecks()).\nSo /healthz and /readyz are served on\nthe METRICS port, separate from the\nproduct APIs and their own /v1/health.\ncurl localhost:9090/healthz is the one\nan operator wants. metricsPath == / is\nhonoured and leaves no room for health." {
    class: go
  }

  join: "RegisterHealth(p *Pipeline)\ningestion/pipeline.go:324\nOne fx.Invoke in ingestion.Module is\nthe whole integration:\nDefaultChecks().Add(Checker{Name:\n'ingestion-storage', Check: p.Check})\np.Check is Pipeline.Err(), which keeps\nthe FIRST failure only, so the probe\nexplains the outage instead of naming\nthe last thing that broke.\nDefaultChecks is a package-level set\nprecisely so that no component has to\ntouch the shared wiring in core/fx.go.\nChecks.Add keeps the first probe of a\nrepeated name, so a component rebuilt\nin a test cannot double-report a\ndependency." {
    class: go
  }

  livez: "GET /healthz — Livez()\nAlways 200, by design: it runs no probe.\nA failing liveness probe restarts a\nprocess that is merely unhealthy, which\nis the opposite of what you want from a\ntrading service. Report carries status,\nservice and uptime_seconds rounded to\nthree places." {
    class: ctl
  }

  readyz: "GET /readyz — Readyz(ctx),\nand this one does fail\nChecks.Run executes every probe\nconcurrently under an RWMutex. The\nfirst result that is not 'ok' sets\nReport.Status = 'degraded' and answers\n503, naming the dependency and its\nerror —\nname=storage status=degraded\nerror='parquet: disk full'\nA nil Check function is itself degraded,\n'no check function'. Anything that is\nneither /healthz nor /readyz is a 404." {
    class: bad
  }

  mux -> livez: "mounted at /"
  mux -> readyz: "the same handler, one branch\nfurther down"
  join -> readyz: "one call, no change to\ncore/fx.go"
}

server: "core/metrics/metrics.go\nthe lifecycle that makes a\nport clash loud" {
  class: lib

  wiring: "core.Module provides metrics.Registry\n— a fresh registry carrying the Go and\nprocess collectors — and metrics.Handler,\nthen fx.Invoke(metrics.Server). Every Go\nservice inherits all three, so a service\ncannot forget to expose /metrics at all." {
    class: go
  }

  onstart: "OnStart binds net.Listen INSIDE\nthe hook, before the goroutine\nA busy cfg.Metrics.Addr returns 'listen\non metrics addr ...' and fx aborts the\napplication. Binding inside the\ngoroutine would log the failure beside a\nprocess that is up, green on /healthz, and\nunscrapeable — the port-collision bug\nclass, made silent. 'metrics server\nlistening' with addr, path and uptime is\nlogged only after the bind has\nsucceeded." {
    class: go
  }

  serve: "go srv.Serve(ln)\nhttp.ErrServerClosed is the normal\nexit and is not logged as an error.\nReadHeaderTimeout 5s, IdleTimeout 60s.\nServer errors go into the same zap\nstream as everything else." {
    class: go
  }

  onstop: "OnStop: srv.Shutdown bounded by\nshutdownTimeout = 5s\nShutdown waits for in-flight scrapes to\nfinish, so the last scrape of a stopping\nprocess still sees a consistent snapshot\nrather than a truncated exposition. The\ntimeout is what stops a wedged scrape\nconnection from holding up application\nshutdown." {
    class: go
  }

  wiring -> onstart
  onstart -> serve: "bound first, then served"
  serve -> onstop: "in flight at stop"
}

logging: "core/log\none encoder decision per process,\none line per request" {
  class: lib

  new: "log.New(cfg *config.Config) — log.go:50\nThe only constructor that reads config,\nand the one fx provides from core/fx.go.\nIt maps app.env, app.log_level and\napp.timezone onto Build(Options), so no\nservice decides its own format.\nBuild(Options) is the constructor for\ntests and for code that is not\nconfig-driven." {
    class: go
  }

  enc: "Format(app.env): dev, development,\nlocal, test -> console with a colourised\nlevel; EVERYTHING ELSE -> JSON. An\nunrecognised environment is production\non purpose — a stack trace pasted into a\nchat is a far smaller problem than a\ncredential on a terminal.\nParseLevel: debug, info, warn, error. An\nunknown value is a startup error, not a\nwarning; empty means info.\napp.timezone drives EncodeTime with\nlayout 2006-01-02T15:04:05.000Z07:00, so\na log line and a candle are read against\nthe same clock. An empty or unresolvable\nzone falls back instead of failing: a\nscratch container with no tzdata must not\nrefuse to trade.\nStack traces on errors and nowhere\nelse." {
    class: go
  }

  envbug: "the bug that fixed this signature\nlog.New used to take a string, and fx\nmatched it to ConfigPath's string return\n— so the config PATH was bound to the\nenvironment parameter. Format saw\n'configs/config.yaml', matched no dev\ncase, returned JSON, and every service\nlogged prod-format JSON regardless of\napp.env. New takes *config.Config now,\nwhich no string provider can satisfy.\nThe parameter type IS the fix." {
    class: ctl
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  mw: "Middleware(logger) — middleware.go:66\nX-Request-Id is read from the inbound\nrequest when present, else\nNewCorrelationID() — 16 bytes of\ncrypto/rand, hex encoded, because a\nguessable request id is an id that can\nbe forged into a log line. It is echoed\non the response and put on the request\ncontext.\nEXACTLY one line per request, chosen\nby status: 5xx Error, 4xx Warn, everything\nelse Debug. Fields: correlation_id ·\nmethod · uri · status · bytes · duration ·\nremote_addr (port stripped).\nuri is redactString(r.URL.RequestURI()),\nnever the raw URI." {
    class: lib
  }

  new -> enc: "app.env · app.log_level ·\napp.timezone"
  new -> envbug: "read this before changing\nthe parameter"
  new -> redact.wrap: "Build wraps the core — there is\nno constructor that returns a\nlogger which does not redact"
}

redact: "core/log/redact.go\nthe wrapper every logger\npasses through" {
  class: lib

  wrap: "redactingCore wraps the zapcore.Core\nit was built on, so this is the LAST line\nof defence rather than the first: a caller\nmay hand it a whole config struct, or a\nbroker error that echoes the request URL.\nWith redacts the accumulated fields, and\nCheck is overridden so every entry is\nrouted through Write — the embedded\nimplementation would pass the original\nfields straight to the wrapped core and\nskip redaction entirely.\nThe walk is bounded so that a log call\ncan never hang a trading process: maxDepth\n8, past which the value is [REDACTED]; a\npointer cycle becomes [cycle]; a byte\nslice is data and is left alone; and\nanything that renders itself — Stringer,\nTextMarshaler, json.Marshaler, error,\nObjectMarshaler, ArrayMarshaler — is\npassed through untouched so timestamps,\ndurations and hand-written marshalers keep\ntheir normal rendering. It is reflection,\nmeant for config and request-scoped\nvalues, not for a per-tick hot loop." {
    class: go
  }

  keys: "IsSensitiveKey(key) — precedence,\nand this is all of it\nnormaliseKey lowercases and keeps only\nalphanumerics, so api_secret, apiSecret\nand API-SECRET are one key.\n1. notSensitive wins over every rule below\n2. sensitiveExact:\n   token · auth · pass · signature · pin\n3. sensitiveSubstrings, matched with\n   Contains:\n   secret · password · passwd · passphrase ·\n   credential · accesstoken · refreshtoken ·\n   idtoken · authtoken · bearer · apikey ·\n   privatekey · authorization · cookie ·\n   sessionkey · otp\nStruct fields are keyed by their WIRE\nname — json tag, then yaml tag, then the\nGo field name — so what reaches the log\nis what the YAML file shows." {
    class: go
  }

  anycfg: "the requirement:\nzap.Any(\"config\", cfg) is safe\nlogger.Info('starting', zap.Any(\"config\",\ncfg)) renders the whole config with\nbroker.api_key, broker.api_secret and\nbroker.access_token each replaced by\n[REDACTED]. The key names stay visible,\nand so do the values you actually need:\ninstruments RELIANCE and TCS,\nstorage.data_dir 'data',\nexecution.capital 1000000.\nA redactor that destroys the line is not\na control — it is a way to guarantee\nnobody reads the log." {
    class: lib
  }

  strings: "redactString — the same keys,\napplied to free text\n1. 'bearer' or 'basic' followed by a\n   token; group 1 keeps the scheme\n2. any key in the class followed by : or\n   = and a value — this is what catches\n   api_secret=…, access_token: … in JSON,\n   and password: …\n3. a query string: ?access_token=…&next=value;\n   group 1 keeps the ?access_token=\nOne replacement template covers all three:\ngroup 1 plus [REDACTED], with the\ncredential left ungrouped. A bare JWT —\neyJ header.payload.signature — is redacted\nin any context. Redaction is idempotent\nby construction, because the credential\ncharacter class excludes '[' so an\nalready-redacted value can never be\nmatched again." {
    class: go
  }

  errs: "redactField — by key first,\nthen by content\nA field whose KEY is sensitive is\nreplaced wholesale whatever its type, so\nzap.String('access_token', ...) is already\n[REDACTED] before its value is even looked\nat. Then by type: String and ByteString\ngo through redactString; Error becomes\nzap.String(redactString(err.Error()))\nbecause a broker error carries the request\nURL, which carries the token — and '403\nfor order 4412' still arrives intact;\nReflect, ObjectMarshaler and ArrayMarshaler\nare walked by Redact. The error case is\nwhat keeps redaction from destroying the\none line that explains the outage." {
    class: go
  }

  exempt: "notSensitive — the exemptions\nare deliberate\ninstrument_token · token_bucket ·\ntoken_bucket_remaining · idempotency_key ·\npublic_key · key_id · cache_key · fluxkv_key ·\ndebounce_key · metric_name · partition_key ·\npartition_by\nThese carry a sensitive word without\ncarrying a credential. Redacting\nidempotency_key would destroy exactly\nwhat you need when debugging a duplicate\norder — it is the one field that explains\nwhy a retried signal was refused — and\nredacting instrument_token would blank\nthe market data. The costs are real, so\nthey are listed by name instead of being\nleft to a heuristic." {
    class: ctl
  }

  wrap -> keys
  keys -> anycfg: "walked by wire name"
  keys -> strings: "the same rules, applied to\nthe message itself"
  keys -> exempt: "checked first,\nand it wins"
  strings -> errs
}

obs: "observability/\ntwo containers and a catalogue, none of\nit in the trading path" {
  class: ext

  prom: "observability/prometheus/prometheus.yml\nscrape_interval 15s · scrape_timeout 10s ·\nevaluation_interval 15s\nexternal_labels: platform=mft\njobs: prometheus(localhost:9090) ·\ningestion :9090 · execution :9091 ·\njobs :9092 · inference :8000, every one\nmetrics_path /metrics.\nThe four services run on the host (make\ndev), so the targets are\nhost.docker.internal, mapped onto the\nhost gateway by\ndocker-compose.observability.yml — the\nonly reason that name resolves on Linux.\nPrometheus is published on 127.0.0.1:9099,\nnot 9090: 9090 is ingestion's metrics\nport." {
    class: ext
  }

  down: "GAP — the inference target\nis permanently DOWN\nThe FastAPI service registers no mft_\nmetric and serves no /metrics endpoint\nat all. The target is declared anyway, on\npurpose: the file's own comment says the\njob exists 'so the target shows up as DOWN\nand the gap is visible, rather than\nbeing silently missing'. A target that is\nabsent cannot be noticed; a red one gets\nasked about." {
    class: bad
  }

  inert: "and MFT_METRICS_ADDR=:9090 for\ninference is inert for the same reason\nMakefile:116 sets it for run-inference in\nmake dev, where it duplicates ingestion's\nport, and a Python process has nothing\nreading it. The same variable is set for\nthe three Go services, which do honour\nit." {
    class: ctl
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  grafana: "grafana/dashboards/mft-overview.json,\nprovisioned by grafana/provisioning —\none screen, four rows, nothing to click\nthrough.\n1. Ingestion: is the data flowing? Tick\n   rate at zero during market hours is\n   the most important signal on the page\n2. Execution: is it trading, and why not —\n   rejections split by reason\n3. Risk headroom, each panel against its\n   configured limit\n4. Platform: what is actually running\nPanels for metrics no component has\nregistered yet are EMPTY, not zero — a\nmissing panel is a visible gap, a fabricated\nzero is a lie you will act on." {
    class: ext
  }

  catalogue: "METRICS.md — the catalogue,\nand the contract\nSix rules: the mft_ prefix; mft_ plus\nsubsystem, noun and verb; units in the\nname (_duration_seconds, _inr, _pct, and\n_pct means 0-100 never 0-1); counters\nend _total; a Help string is mandatory;\nbounded labels only — never a correlation\nid, an order id or a timestamp — with\nObserveDuration named as the one sanctioned\nway to attach one.\n⧗ marks a metric nobody has registered\nyet and names its owner." {
    class: ctl
  }

  stale: "but the catalogue has drifted\nfrom the tree\nIts 'Metrics that violate the prefix'\ntable still lists four unprefixed names —\ningestion_ticks_processed_total,\nexecution_orders_placed_total,\nexecution_orders_rejected_total,\njobs_backfills_run_total. All four have\nsince been renamed, the last one to\nmft_jobs_backfill_runs_total.\nThe dashboard makes two queries of the\nsame class: mft_http_requests_total where\nexecution registers\nmft_execution_http_requests_total, and\nmft_ingestion_candles_written_total where\ningestion registers\nmft_ingestion_candles_completed_total.\nBoth panels read no data." {
    class: ctl
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  prom -> down
  down -> inert: "one gap, two places\nit shows"
  prom -> grafana: "PromQL, every 15s"
  catalogue -> grafana: "a new metric means a new\nrow here too"
  catalogue -> stale: "which no longer describes\nthe tree"
}

wiring -> validate: "the one *prometheus.Registry\n every constructor\n registers on"
validate -> buildinfo: "RegisterBuildInfo validates\n mft_build_info too — and\n returns the error instead of\n panicking"
serve -> prom: "scrape /metrics on four ports"
mw -> observe: "X-Request-Id ->\nObserveDuration(h, start, id) ->\nthe trace_id exemplar Prometheus\nstores next to the bucket"
nocall -> grafana: "so the Platform row's build\npanels have no series"

footer: "Derived from:\ncore/metrics/naming.go — Prefix mft_, DurationSuffix, ErrMissingPrefix, ValidateName,\nValidateDurationName, newSpec, newDurationSpec, must, MustRegister, the eight constructors\ncore/metrics/latency.go — DefaultBuckets, DurationHistogram, DurationHistogramVec, ObserveDuration\ncore/metrics/buildinfo.go — BuildInfo, RegisterBuildInfo, readBuildStamps, processStart\ncore/metrics/health.go — Checker, Checks.Add and Run, DefaultChecks, NewHealth, Livez, Readyz, ServeHTTP\ncore/metrics/metrics.go — Registry, Handler, Mux, metricsPath, Server, shutdownTimeout\ncore/metrics/server_test.go — TestServerFailsLoudlyOnABusyPort\ncore/fx.go — log.New, metrics.Registry, metrics.Handler, fx.Invoke(metrics.Server), ConfigPath\ncore/log/log.go — New, Build, encoderConfig, Format, ParseLevel, location, timeLayout\ncore/log/redact.go — Redacted, maxDepth, sensitiveSubstrings, sensitiveExact, notSensitive,\nIsSensitiveKey, normaliseKey, Redact, redactString, secretPatterns, tokenPattern,\nredactingCore.Check/Write/With, redactField\ncore/log/redact_test.go — TestRedactConfigStruct, TestRedactLeavesUsefulValuesAlone, TestRedactingCoreIsInTheChain\ncore/log/middleware.go — RequestIDHeader, NewCorrelationID, WithCorrelationID, Middleware\ncore/config/config.go — app.env, app.log_level, app.timezone, metrics.addr, metrics.path\nservices/ingestion/pipeline.go — Module, RegisterHealth, Check, Err, newMetrics\nservices/execution/http.go, services/execution/engine.go — the mft_ names the dashboard queries\nobservability/prometheus/prometheus.yml · observability/METRICS.md · observability/README.md\nobservability/grafana/dashboards/mft-overview.json · Makefile:112-116, 195-222" {
  class: ctl
  style.fill: "#ffffff"
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}
